**Quality: Concurrent Access Safety**
```rust
pub struct ProjectManager {
    projects: Arc<RwLock<HashMap<String, ProjectHandle>>>,
    current_project: Arc<RwLock<Option<String>>>,
    storage_configs: Arc<RwLock<HashMap<String, StorageConfig>>>,
}
```
- **Why RwLock?** Multiple concurrent reads, exclusive writes
- **Why Arc?** Safe sharing across async tasks
- **Failure Mode**: Lock poisoning handled gracefully, returns error instead of panic

**Quality: Storage Layout (Flexible per Project)**

Projects can store data **anywhere** - not just globally:

```
# Option 1: Global storage (centralized)
~/.specd/
├── config.ini                    # specd global config
└── projects/
    ├── default/
    │   ├── config.ini            # Project config
    │   ├── udaf-model.json
    │   ├── nodes/
    │   └── edges.yaml
    └── my-web-app/
        ├── config.ini
        ├── udaf-model.json
        ├── nodes/
        └── edges.yaml

# Option 2: Local storage (project-local .spec/ - existing pattern)
/path/to/my-project/
├── .spec/
│   ├── config.ini                # Project config
│   ├── udaf-model.json
│   ├── nodes/
│   └── edges.yaml
└── src/
    └── ...

# Option 3: Remote storage (S3, Database, etc.)
# (Config stored locally, data stored remotely)
~/.specd/projects/my-app/
└── config.ini                    # Points to s3://bucket/my-app/

# Option 4: Git repository
~/.specd/projects/my-app/
└── config.ini                    # Points to github.com/org/specs.git
```

**Configuration Files (INI format):**

`~/.specd/config.ini`:
```ini
[specd]
listen_address = [::1]:50051
log_level = info

[projects]
default_storage = local
default_path = ~/.specd/projects
```

`~/.spec/config.ini` (spec-cli global config):
```ini
[spec]
default_server = http://[::1]:50051
output_format = pretty
color = auto

[ai]
provider = claude
model = claude-sonnet-4
```

Project config (e.g., `.spec/config.ini` or `~/.specd/projects/my-app/config.ini`):
```ini
[project]
name = my-web-app
description = Web application specifications
created_at = 2025-02-15T10:30:00Z

[storage]
backend = local
path = .

; Alternative: Remote storage
; [storage]
; backend = postgres
; connection_string = postgresql://localhost/specd
; schema = public

; Alternative: S3 storage
; [storage]
; backend = s3
; bucket = my-company-specs
; prefix = projects/my-web-app
; region = us-west-2
```

Project decides:
- **Where**: Local `.spec/`, global `~/.specd/projects/`, remote S3/DB/Git
- **How**: LocalFile, Database, S3, Git
- **When**: At project creation time, persisted in `config.ini`

**Migration Support for Existing .spec/ Directories:**
- Existing `.spec/` directories remain valid
- No forced migration to global storage
- User can choose: keep local, move to global, or migrate to remote
- `spec project import` respects original location or moves to specified backend

